Multan Sultans (Urdu/Saraiki/Punjabi: ملتان سلطانز) are a professional Twenty20 franchise cricket team based in Multan, Punjab, that competes in the Pakistan Super League (PSL). The team is currently owned by Gohar Shah of CD Ventures who bought the Sialkot Stallionz franchise in 2026 and rebranded it to Multan Sultans. Their home ground is the Multan Cricket Stadium.
Multan Sultans had won their first PSL title in the 2021 season by defeating Peshawar Zalmi in the final. The franchise reached the finals in four consecutive seasons between 2021 and 2024, winning once and finishing runners-up three times, establishing itself as one of the PSL's most consistent teams.
